# Does the priest spell Heal, cast by the PLAYER himself, cure all nine
# non-PARALYSIS maladies its "and EA_HEALING" clauses name? Read by
# tools/check_heal_maladies.sh. bd inc-xr8i.
#
# THE NINE: BLIND, CONFUSED, DISEASED, STUNNED, POISONED, HALLU, BLEEDING,
# CHOKING, WOUNDED. The second half of this file measures those nine on the
# PLAYER, afflicted directly by the test god below. PARALYSIS is a separate,
# later design decision (bd inc-pfmv) and cannot be measured that way -- a
# paralysed character cannot cast Heal on himself. It is measured instead,
# on a different creature, in the FIRST half of this file, below.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: the paralysis half runs BEFORE the nine-malady half, on
# purpose. The nine-malady god blinds and stuns the player among other
# things, and a blind player cannot perceive or target a kobold at all --
# Q_TAR skips anything unperceived (tools/keys/breath-dice-dragon.keys has
# the same note about a dragon's shadow). Proving this file red (the mutation
# that deletes every "and EA_HEALING" malady clause, including PARALYSIS'S)
# leaves the player blind, stunned and confused for the rest of the session,
# because that same mutation breaks the nine-malady cure too. Running the
# paralysis half first means it never has to survive that.
#
# THE ROUTE, in two halves.
#
#   Half one, PARALYSIS: summons a kobold, casts Hold Person at it, confirms
#   the hold, casts the same innate Heal at it instead of at the player, and
#   confirms the cure. See the header above that half for the file:line
#   evidence.
#
#   Half two, THE NINE: tools/fixtures/heal-maladies-god.irh, spliced onto a
#   scratch copy of lib/main.irc by the check script (never onto the tracked
#   lib/), declares one test god. "Become Divine Champion" (wizard mode)
#   joins it and grants 30000 favour outright (src/Debug.cpp), which fires
#   its EV_BLESSING once; the handler calls GainPermStati directly for all
#   nine maladies, the same call lib/religion.irh:5958 (Zurvash) makes. No
#   ThrowEff, no scripted spell throw: GainPermStati is not the spell, it is
#   a shortcut to the AFFLICTION only, so that the CURE below is still the
#   real thing, cast by the player. Then wizard "Learn Any Spell" teaches
#   "Heal;spell" (lib/pspells.irh's Priest / Scroll Spell) as an innate
#   ability, and [u] Innate Heal, ENTER casts it on the default target --
#   himself. An innate cast always succeeds (Character::SpellRating returns
#   100 for SP_INNATE, src/Magic.cpp:3188-3191) and costs no mana.
#
# THE ORACLE, both halves: wizard debug Dump() (src/Debug.cpp) prints an
# unfiltered "Stati (n):" list naming every active status by its full
# constant name via STATI_CONSTNAMES (src/Tables.cpp) -- unlike the
# right-hand status panel, which shows at most one malady at a time behind an
# if/else-if priority chain (src/Term.cpp:426-444) and never mentions HALLU,
# BLEEDING, CHOKING or WOUNDED at all, and cannot show more than one creature
# at once regardless. The dump scrolls; ten DOWN presses were measured
# (tools/fixtures/heal-maladies-god.irh's own header run) to bring the whole
# nine-entry block on screen from a fresh, top-scrolled entry, because
# entering the screen calls ClearScroll(true) each time and resets the
# scroll position. Do NOT scroll further: past the end of a Dump()'s
# content, this debug view's scroller segfaults (observed 2026-09-17,
# unrelated to any of the maladies here -- reproduced by continuing to press
# DOWN after the last line of output already showed. Not filed: src/ is off
# limits for this bead and the view is a wizard/debug tool, not
# player-facing).
#
# WHY NOT THE STATUS PANEL: it is a single priority-ordered line (Paralyzed >
# Poisoned > Diseased > Stunned > Sickly > Confused > Blind), so afflicting
# all nine at once would only ever show ONE name there, and it structurally
# cannot show HALLU, BLEEDING, CHOKING or WOUNDED under any affliction.
#
# EMPIRICAL RESULT ON THE BLOCKING-MALADY TRAP: tried, not assumed. One
# single run affects the player with all nine simultaneously -- including
# STUNNED, CONFUSED and BLIND -- then teaches and casts Heal in the same run
# with no split needed. The wizard-mode menu commands and the innate cast
# both went through untouched: HP stayed 42/42 across the run (no bleed or
# choke damage: the fixture pins Val/Mag to 0), the cast produced "You feel
# fully refreshed!", and the after-dump showed all nine gone. Nothing here
# forced a per-malady run.

@include chargen.keys

w
y                       # Enter wizard mode? [yn] -- only asked once

# FIRST MEASUREMENT: PARALYSIS. A paralysed character cannot act, so he
# cannot cast Heal on himself -- the patient and the caster must be two
# different creatures.
#
# THE MONSTER: a kobold, summoned nearby. It is MA_PERSON (M_HUMANOID, Size
# SMALL, not fey/undead/mindless -- src/Values.cpp:2512-2525), which Hold
# Person requires (tval: MA_PERSON, lib/wspells.irh:4435). Its Will save is
# POOR: MA_KOBOLD saves only Reflex, never Will (src/Values.cpp:2232-2240,
# MonGoodSaves). Seed 2 (this file's own seed, see the check script's own
# header) fails the kobold's save every time this was tried; seed 1 let it
# succeed, which is why the seed is pinned rather than left to whatever the
# caller passes.
#
# THE HOLD: "Learn Any Spell" teaches Hold Person as an innate ability, cast
# through 'm' (the same route tools/keys/zeal-strike.keys uses for Zeal) at
# the kobold one square east. The Q_TAR prompt defaults its cursor onto the
# caster's own square, so RIGHT then ENTER moves it onto the kobold and
# confirms -- the same two keys zeal-strike.keys uses for the same reason.
#
# THE ORACLE: wizard "Examine Nearby Things" (Player::BrowseThings, true),
# which opens on the player's own entry and cycles with RIGHT/LEFT through
# everything within 10 squares. One RIGHT reaches the kobold -- it is the
# only other thing that close.
#
# THE CURE: "Learn Any Spell" teaches "Heal;spell", then the same 'u' Innate
# Heal route the nine-malady half below uses, but RIGHT then ENTER targets
# the kobold instead of taking the self default.
#
# FREEZE MONSTERS FIRST (the eleventh row of the Wizard Mode Switches list,
# same DOWN*10 SPACE ESC route tools/keys/zeal-strike.keys uses): a summoned
# kobold that keeps its activity cycle gets a turn between these menu
# commands and can attack, which derailed an earlier version of this script
# into a combat prompt neither @choose nor @dump expected. Freezing does not
# skip the kobold's saving throw against Hold Person -- only its own turns.
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Kobolds"
@choose "kobold"
RIGHT
ENTER

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Hold Person" ENTER

m
@choose "Hold Person"
RIGHT
ENTER

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
RIGHT
DOWN*10                # scroll the debug dump down to the Stati block
@dump:para-hold
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Heal;spell" ENTER

u
@choose "Innate Heal"
RIGHT
ENTER

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
RIGHT
DOWN*10
@dump:para-cure
ESC

# SECOND MEASUREMENT: THE NINE, on the player himself. See the file header.
w
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
"Heal Maladies Test God" ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*10                # scroll the debug dump down to the Stati block
@dump:control
ESC

u
@choose "Innate Heal"
ENTER                   # confirm the default target: self -- already known

w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*10                # same fixed scroll: ClearScroll(true) reset it to top
@dump:after
ESC

@quit
